# sportlogic-php

PHP client for the [SportLogic Virtual Racing API](https://sportlogic.io). PHP 8.1+, no dependencies beyond curl and json.

The API returns virtual racing data as JSON over REST: scheduled and finished events, runners with draw numbers and form, win and place odds, and results with win, place, forecast and tricast settlement. It covers 8 racing game types across six sports: [virtual horse racing](https://sportlogic.io/integrations/virtual-horse-racing-api), [greyhound racing](https://sportlogic.io/integrations/virtual-greyhound-racing-api), [harness racing](https://sportlogic.io/integrations/virtual-harness-racing-api), [steeplechase](https://sportlogic.io/integrations/virtual-steeplechase-api), [motor racing](https://sportlogic.io/integrations/virtual-motor-racing-api) and [speed skating](https://sportlogic.io/integrations/virtual-speed-skating-api).

The free plan is $0 with 500 requests a day. No credit card. Get a key at [dashboard.sportlogic.io](https://dashboard.sportlogic.io).

## Install

Add the repository to your `composer.json`, then require the package:

```json
{
    "repositories": [
        { "type": "vcs", "url": "https://github.com/sportlogic-io/sportlogic-php" }
    ]
}
```

```bash
composer require sportlogic-io/sportlogic-php:dev-main
```

## Quick start

```php
use SportLogic\Client;

$client = new Client(apiKey: getenv('SPORTLOGIC_API_KEY'));

// List scheduled events
$page = $client->events(status: 'scheduled');
$events = $page['data'];

// One event with runners, draw numbers, odds and form
$detail = $client->event($events[0]['id']);

// Results and settlement after the race finishes
$results = $client->eventResults($events[0]['id']);
```

## Methods

| Method | Endpoint |
| --- | --- |
| `health()` | `GET /health` (no key needed) |
| `gameTypes()` | `GET /game-types` |
| `gameTypeInfo($id)` | `GET /game-types/{id}/info` |
| `markets()` | `GET /markets` |
| `events(...)` | `GET /events` |
| `event($id)` | `GET /events/{id}` |
| `eventResults($id, ...)` | `GET /events/{id}/results` |
| `usage()` | `GET /usage` |

## Pagination

`events()` is cursor-paginated. Pass `pagination['next_cursor']` back as `$cursor` to get the next page.

```php
$page = $client->events(perPage: 50);
while ($page['pagination'] && $page['pagination']['has_more']) {
    $page = $client->events(perPage: 50, cursor: $page['pagination']['next_cursor']);
}
```

## Errors

Failed requests throw `SportLogic\SportLogicException` with `status`, `errorCode`, `requestId` and `docUrl`.

```php
use SportLogic\SportLogicException;

try {
    $client->eventResults($eventId);
} catch (SportLogicException $e) {
    if ($e->status === 400) {
        // Event has not finished yet
    }
}
```

## Save your quota

Cache responses by event id while you build. A settled result never changes, so cache results for as long as you like. Fetch the schedule on a timer, not on every page load.

